      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Amino acids provide the nitrogen components, while reducing sugars act as the electrophiles in the initial Maillard reaction. They react to form unstable intermediates, such as Schiff bases, which are the starting points for browning products. pH significantly influences the reaction rate because the ionization state of both the amino acids and sugars affects their reactivity; generally, the Maillard reaction proceeds fastest under slightly alkaline conditions.",
