      "content": "The transformation from Schiff bases to melanoidins involves a cascade of complex chemical mechanisms, primarily condensation, cyclization, and subsequent polymerization. These initial adducts undergo Amadori rearrangement, leading to more stable, ketoamine-like compounds. Subsequently, these intermediates decompose via Strecker degradation or other fragmentation pathways, resulting in smaller flavor-contributing molecules, which then react further to form the large, dark polymers known as melanoidins.",
